course: dictionary
lesson: 3348
title: The examen: a daily look back
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show which meaning is right. «Christians practise looking back over the day: give thanks and notice where you went wrong.» Words like give thanks and wrong point to prayer, so examen here means a religious habit, not a school test.
explain: In church, the examen is a short daily prayer. A person looks back over the day, thanks God for good things, and asks forgiveness for wrong ones. Ignatius of Loyola taught this prayer in the 1500s, and it is often prayed at bedtime.
explain: Watch out for French. In French lessons, «examen» means an exam or test. In an English lesson about prayer, the clues tell you it means the church prayer. Always check: does my meaning fit the words around it?
fact: The examen is a short daily prayer.
fact: In the examen, a person looks back over the day, thanks God for good things, and asks forgiveness for wrong ones.
fact: The examen comes from Saint Ignatius of Loyola, who taught it in the 1500s.
fact: In French, «examen» means an exam or test, but it is not an ordinary English word in that sense.
fact: An examination (old, formal) means a careful study.
exercise: «Christians practise looking back over the day: give thanks and notice where you went wrong.» What is the examen? | A journey to a far-off place | A French test for school | A kind of church music | *A short daily prayer that looks back over the day
exercise: In the examen, what does a person do? | Writes a school report | *Looks back over the day and thanks God for good things | Counts coins for the collection | Sings a loud song at a football match
exercise: Who taught the examen, according to the sentences? | Lamentations | A Scottish grandad | A French teacher | *Ignatius of Loyola
test: In an English prayer lesson, what does «examen» usually mean? | A school exam in maths | *A short daily prayer | A long walk in the hills
test: What does the old word examination mean? | *A careful study | A picnic lunch | A loud argument
exam: «Examen» is in a sentence about «the Lord» and «give thanks». What does this clue show? | It is a sports word, so it means a game | It is a French word, so it means an exam | It is a food word, so it means a meal | *It is a religious word, so it means a church prayer
